maintenance_help: 0
usage: uns-maintain [-h] [--database-url DATABASE_URL] --cutoff CUTOFF
                    --idempotency-seconds IDEMPOTENCY_SECONDS
                    [--batch-size BATCH_SIZE] [--apply] [--operator OPERATOR]
                    [--after-id AFTER_ID] [--archive ARCHIVE]

Explicit, bounded retention for SQLite notification stores. Nothing runs at
startup. The operator chooses both the inactivity cutoff and the minimum
idempotency window. Expiring an outbox row expires its idempotency key; a
subsequent request with that key may create a new notification. Without an
archive, events and delivery/ACK audits remain in the database and the removal
receipt preserves the removed operational rows. With an archive, whole settled
notification groups are exported, fsynced, hash-verified, then pruned in one
SQLite writer transaction. Policy history and retention receipts are never
pruned. This reuses database pages; it does not shrink the SQLite file or
establish an audit/compliance retention policy. Oversized groups are kept.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --database-url DATABASE_URL
  --cutoff CUTOFF
  --idempotency-seconds IDEMPOTENCY_SECONDS
  --batch-size BATCH_SIZE
  --apply               Commit one bounded batch
  --operator OPERATOR   Attribution required for --apply
  --after-id AFTER_ID   Continue after a returned next_after_id; omit to start
                        a new pass
  --archive ARCHIVE     New archive file in a trusted existing directory

